.Dd February 1, 2026
.Dt SPINLOCK 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm spinlock_init ,
.Nm spinlock_acquire ,
.Nm spinlock_release ,
.Nm spinlock_try_acquire
.Nd busy-wait synchronization primitive
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/lock.h
.Ft void
.Fn spinlock_init "spinlock_t *sl" "const char *name"
.Ft void
.Fn spinlock_acquire "spinlock_t *sl"
.Ft void
.Fn spinlock_release "spinlock_t *sl"
.Ft int
.Fn spinlock_try_acquire "spinlock_t *sl"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Spinlocks provide mutual exclusion for short critical sections, typically in interrupt handlers or scheduler code where sleeping is not permitted.
.Pp
.Fn spinlock_acquire
busy-waits until the lock is available. It disables local interrupts while holding the lock to prevent deadlocks with interrupt handlers on the same CPU.
.Pp
.Fn spinlock_release
releases the lock and restores the previous interrupt state.
.Pp
.Fn spinlock_try_acquire
attempts to acquire the lock without spinning.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn spinlock_try_acquire
returns 1 if the lock was acquired, 0 otherwise.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mutex 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn spinlock
primitive first appeared in Substrate.
